{"kind":"report","text":"VERDICT: changes-requested at exact head 4981c6d0f571c9a7504311f83c6cb08517be0acd on request/receipt-checkpoint-freshness, answering request da51231d2db2102ee5365ce417e8f6949646420b under the ratified ruling 2210e4ea0311efc4eccfff9d3a2c4463ea12f3d6.\n\nCONFIRMED, examinations 1-3, 5, 7. (1) The gate and temporal rule match the ruling: settlement only for causes dated at or before the receipt sequence unless plan-named; the walk starts at the receipt so its own retirement still flares; the receipt keeps its historical staleness; left-live verification is never read. (2) Undated causes fail closed (the when==0 arm refuses settlement) and the dedicated white-box test pins that arm. (3) The checkpoint fires only on the direct successor-cites-receipt basis; describes_superseded_world is untouched in every branch because a receipt is an assert and can never carry artifact provenance on that edge. (5) Both white-box tests are justified: parse-order coupling and the retirement-counter cascade make their states unreachable through Fold, and mutation runs show each catches a defect the through-Fold half cannot see. (7) ProfileVersion workroom-fold@12 changes the composite snapshot profile key and forces replay; reverting it in a mutated copy makes TestAnOlderProfileCacheIsRebuiltUnderTheNewRules fail, so the rebuilt-cache test genuinely discriminates.\n\nTESTS, all green at the exact tree: gofmt clean; go build ./..., go vet ./..., git diff --check clean; go test -count=1 ./internal/workroom/... ./internal/app/... green; full go test -count=1 ./... completed within budget, 31 packages, zero failures. Mutation experiments (paired-fields, left-live half, same-author, date cutoff, nil-plan, added verification-read, profile revert) confirm every key guard individually load-bearing.\n\nEXAMINATION 6 FAILS, and that is the requested change. On the live log, at identical frontiers, binaries built at main 72c3b724dbf5919a59a8ae7aefe6c9ba3d209605 and at this head emit byte-identical inspect output for both published successors of receipt 03c440d40e4da28f2673f607248294f3a62323cc (13c9a0a2861529a51aacfc20bf721135f951fe25 at cmd/gs and 1fb4d37a6a54a73df67311e9f2967bfecba535d1 at docs): stale true under BOTH binaries, where the condition expected stale under the former and current under the latter. Independent forensics say the checkpoint should fire here: every gate verifiably holds from the signed bodies and provenance (prospective pair present with canonical merge_changed_paths; sealed four-entry merge_retirements plan; successor and receipt share author; commit equals merge_head 72c3b724dbf5919a59a8ae7aefe6c9ba3d209605; paths cmd/gs and docs are declared merge_successors; the successor rests on the receipt alone); every unplanned retirement in the receipt closure predates the receipt (latest effective unplanned act sequence 11376 \u003c 11567); and the only post-receipt retirements in the closure are exactly the four plan-named predecessor withdrawals. By the ruling and by the shipped fixtures own semantics the settled-walk should answer true; the fold answers false, and no shipped fixture reproduces the decline, so its precise site is not yet isolated. Root-causing that divergence is the requested change; please add a regression fixture built from the real receipts field shape so this class of real-log decline cannot ship invisible again.\n\nArchitecture: layer 5 ownership is right (internal/workroom/fold.go staleness computation; kernel and CLI untouched) and the three contract pages are updated in the same head; but the freshness contract the pages document demonstrably does not hold on the live log for the exemplar pair the ruling itself names, so the contract is written but not delivered. Security: fail-closed throughout; the defect keeps artifacts conservatively stale and never falsely fresh; authorship, exact-head, declared-path, undated, malformed-pair and borrower gates all verified against real events plus mutation; no security defect found. Simplification: nothing to cut without weakening conditions; the two white-box tests earn their keep; the only ask is the added regression fixture above.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0c0c5bcedaf44887727b22615d378fdaf6787d5f","head":"4981c6d0f571c9a7504311f83c6cb08517be0acd","verdict":"changes-requested"}}